  "worked_solution": "The equation of the regression line is given by\n\n$$\ny=mx+b,\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{S}_{xy}}{{S}_{xx}},\\,b=\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $m:$\n\n- First, we compute the sum in the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xy} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})({y}_{i}-\\overset{―}{y}) \\\\  & =(1-2)(71-74)+(2-2)(75-74) \\\\  & +(1-2)(65-74)+(4-2)(85-74) \\\\  & =(-1)(-3)+(0)(1)+(-1)(-9)+(2)(11) \\\\  & =3+0+9+22 \\\\  & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Second, we compute the sum in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{xx} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-\\overset{―}{x})^{2} \\\\  & =(1-2)^{2}+(2-2)^{2}+(1-2)^{2}+(4-2)^{2} \\\\  & =1+0+1+4 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for $m,$ we obtain \n\n$$\nm=\\frac{34}{6}=\\frac{17}{3}≈5.667.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute into the formula for $b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b & =\\overset{―}{y}-m\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =74-\\frac{17}{3}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{188}{3} \\\\  & ≈62.667\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the regression line is\n\n$$\ny=5.667x+62.667.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can predict the average grade of a student that studies $3$ hours per day by substituting $x=3$ into our regression line:\n\n$$\ny=5.667(3)+62.667≈80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the model predicts that a student that studies three hours per day will have an average grade of $80$ points.",
